.TP
.B USER
Login name from the utmp entry.
.TP
.B TTY
Controlling terminal of the session (\fItty2\fR, \fIpts/0\fR,
\fIseat0\fR for desktop seat managers, etc.).
.TP
.B FROM
(\fB\-f\fR only) Where the session was initiated from: remote
hostname or IP address for SSH connections, the display name for
graphical sessions, "login screen" for the GDM/SDDM greeter slot.
With \fB\-i\fR, hostnames are replaced by IP addresses verbatim.
.TP
.B LOGIN@
Time the user logged in. Same-day logins are shown as
\fIHH:MM\fR; older logins use a short weekday format like
\fITue11\fR. Omitted under \fB\-s\fR.
.TP
.B IDLE
Time since the controlling terminal was last active. Formats vary by
magnitude: seconds (\fI29.00s\fR), minutes (\fI1:51m\fR), hours
(\fI17:51m\fR), days (\fI4days\fR), or \fB?\fR if the tty's idle time
cannot be read. With \fB\-o\fR, idle times below one minute are
shown as a blank cell instead of seconds.
.TP
.B JCPU
"Job CPU" — total CPU time consumed by every process attached to
this session's tty, summed across active and ended children.
Omitted under \fB\-s\fR.
.TP
.B PCPU
"Process CPU" — CPU time consumed by the current foreground process
on this session. With \fB\-u\fR, this is the login process itself.
Omitted under \fB\-s\fR.
.TP
.B WHAT
The command line of the session's foreground process. With \fB\-u\fR,
the login process's command line. With \fB\-p\fR, the values are
prefixed with \fIloginpid\fR\fB/\fR\fIwhatpid\fR.
